  <content>
  <section><title>Identify Positive and Negative Trends </title>
<para dir="ltr">Scatter plots may have a strong linear trend or a weak linear trend. A strong positive trend means as one variable increases, the other variable increases, A strong negative trend means as one variable increases, the other variable decreases. A weak linear pattern means the points are more scattered.  </para>
<para><figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/1c8336136ee63f5d6b6ef99fc081a7ea0506e32e"/></media></figure><emphasis/></para>
<newline/><title><span>Try It: Identify Positive and Negative Trends </span></title>
<para><figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/f363fc1f7e63b16ad602651217bffb9f6a3d45d6"/></media></figure><emphasis/></para>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Does the scatter plot show a positive or negative trend? Is the relationship weak or strong?</para>
  </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  <para>Here is how to describe the relationship:</para>
    <para>As the \(x\)-values increase, the \(y\)-values decrease. The trend is negative. The relationship is linear, but the points are scattered, so the relationship is weak.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--inserted mini review question Begin -->
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Check Your Understanding</title><exercise data-content-id="33592150-3516-4f57-a9e6-6351e6ee7c9a" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>The scatter plot shows the relationship between crocodiles body mass in pounds, \(x\), and bite force in pounds, \(y\). Which statement best describes the relationship between body mass and bite force?</para><para dir="ltr"><b id="docs-internal-guid-5ae9ff7d-7fff-3e96-6f29-e0a5fc1e1f8d"><figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/9a74b1315b2ca91f0badced5dc3cc085f8b912e1"/></media></figure></b></para>
    <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>There appears to be a positive relationship between bite force and body mass. The greater the body mass, the greater the bite force tends to be.</para><para>There appears to be a positive relationship between bite force and body mass. The greater the body mass, the lighter the bite force tends to be.</para><para>There appears to be a negative relationship between bite force and body mass. The greater the body mass, the greater the bite force tends to be.</para><para>There appears to be a negative relationship between bite force and body mass. The greater the body mass, the lighter the bite force tends to be.</para></problem><solution><para>Incorrect. Let’s try again a different way: There does appear to be a positive relationship, but that is because both quantities are increasing. The answer is there appears to be a positive relationship between bite force and body mass. The greater the body mass, the greater the bite force tends to be.</para></solution></exercise></section><!--inserted mini review question END -->
